:"IM_e3tZiBPIiiVzzE1","GraphicsDescription":"wm1659c.jpg","QuestionID":"QID1207"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_aUYX8XjalY6EcDk","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1208","SecondaryAttribute":" ","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https:\/\/virginia.az1.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_ag6DK3heLwAMEyG\" style=\"width: 399px; height: 280px;\" \/><\/div>","QuestionJS":false,"DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q1200","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":" ","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":37,"NextAnswerId":1,"Graphics":"IM_e3tZiBPIiiVzzE1","GraphicsDescription":"wm1659c.jpg","QuestionID":"QID1208"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_aUYX8XjalY6EcDk","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1209","SecondaryAttribute":" ","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https:\/\/virginia.az1.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_ag6DK3heLwAMEyG\" style=\"width: 399px; height: 280px;\" \/><\/div>","QuestionJS":false,"DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q1201","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":" ","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":37,"NextAnswerId":1,"Graphics":"IM_e3tZiBPIiiVzzE1","GraphicsDescription":"wm1659c.jpg","QuestionID":"QID1209"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_aUYX8XjalY6EcDk","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID121","SecondaryAttribute":"You are invited to participate in a research study by Chad Dodson, PhD, from the Department of Ps...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"You are invited to participate in a research study by Chad Dodson, PhD, from the Department of Psychology at the University of Virginia. The study consists of an online survey that should take approximately <strong>60 minutes<\/strong> to complete. Your responses will be kept confidential. You may drop out of the study at any time by closing this browser window. The purpose of this study will be revealed in greater detail once you have completed the survey.&nbsp;<strong>Please read the following consent agreement before continuing:<\/strong><br \/>\n<br \/>\n<strong>Informed Consent Agreement<\/strong><br \/>\n<br \/>\nPage 1 of 1: Project Title: <em>Judging Emotional Expressions in Faces<\/em><br \/>\n&nbsp;&nbsp;<br \/>\nPlease read this consent agreement carefully before you decide to participate in the study.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nPurpose of the research study: The purpose of the study is to investigate how we interpret various facial expressions.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nWhat you will do in the study: You will be asked to make judgments about pictures of faces.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nTime required: The study will require between 5 and 120 minutes of your time, and is expected to take most people 60 minutes to complete.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nRisks: There are no anticipated risks in this study. &nbsp;<br \/>\n<br \/>\nBenefits: There are no direct benefits to you for participating in this research study. &nbsp;<br \/>\n<br \/>\nConfidentiality: The information that you give in the study will be handled confidentially. &nbsp;Your information will be assigned a code number. &nbsp;The list connecting your name to this code will be kept secure. &nbsp;When the study is completed and the data have been analyzed, this list will be destroyed. &nbsp;Your name will not be used in any report.&nbsp;<br \/>\n<br \/>\nVoluntary participation: Your participation in the study is completely voluntary.&nbsp;<br \/>\n<br \/>\nRight to withdraw from the study: You have the right to withdraw from the study at any time without penalty.&nbsp;<br \/>\n<br \/>\nHow to withdraw from the study: If you want to withdraw from the study, please close your web browser. &nbsp;We will not use (and will delete) data from participants who do not complete the study. &nbsp;If you would like to withdraw after your data have been submitted, please contact Craig Gallagher or Emily Ives (see below for contact information). &nbsp;<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<em>Payment: You will receive 1 participation credit for completing this study, which is expected to require 60 minutes of your time. You will not receive less credit for finishing in under an hour, nor will you receive additional participation credit if you require more than 60 minutes to complete the study.<\/em><br \/>\n<br \/>\nIf you have questions about the study, contact:<br \/>\n<br \/>\nCraig Gallagher<br \/>\nUniversity of Virginia, Charlottesville, VA 22904<br \/>\nEmail: rcg7jb@virginia.edu<br \/>\n<br \/>\nand\/or<br \/>\n&nbsp;&nbsp;<br \/>\nEmily Ives<br \/>\nDepartment of Psychology,<br \/>\nBox 400400, Gilmer Hall<br \/>\nUniversity of Virginia, Charlottesville, VA 22904<br \/>\nEmail: xby5us@virginia.edu<br \/>\n<br \/>\nIf you have questions about your rights as a participant in this study, contact:<br \/>\n<br \/>\nTonya R. Moon, Ph.D.,&nbsp;<br \/>\nChair, Institutional Review Board for the Social and Behavioral Sciences<br \/>\nOne Morton Dr Suite 500&nbsp;<br \/>\nUniversity of Virginia, P.O. Box 800392<br \/>\nCharlottesville, VA 22908-0392<br \/>\nTelephone: &nbsp;(434) 924-5999&nbsp;<br \/>\nEmail: irbsbshelp@virginia.edu<br \/>\nWebsite: www.virginia.edu\/vprgs\/irb<br \/>\n<br \/>\nAgreement: By clicking on continue, I agree to participate in the research study described above.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nIf you would like a copy for your records please print this page or save it to a file.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<strong>If you would like to participate please minimize other distractions and then click on the next arrow button:<\/strong>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q114","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"You are invited to participate in a research study by Chad Dodson, PhD, from the Department of Ps...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID121"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_aUYX8XjalY6EcDk","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1210","SecondaryAttribute":" ","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https:\/\/virginia.az1.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_ag6DK3heLwAMEyG\" style=\"width: 399px; height: 280px;\" \/><\/div>","QuestionJS":false,"DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q1202","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":" ","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":37,"NextAnswerId":1,"Graphics":"IM_e3tZiBPIiiVzzE1","GraphicsDescription":"wm1659c.jpg","QuestionID":"QID1210"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_aUYX8XjalY6EcDk","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1211","SecondaryAttribute":" ","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https:\/\/virginia.az1.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_ag6DK3heLwAMEyG\" style=\"width: 399px; height: 280px;\" \/><\/div>","QuestionJS":false,"DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q1203","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":" ","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":37,"NextAnswerId":1,"Graphics":"IM_e3tZiBPIiiVzzE1","GraphicsDescription":"wm1659c.jpg","QuestionID":"QID1211"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_aUYX8XjalY6EcDk","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1212","SecondaryAttribute":" ","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https:\/\/virginia.az1.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_eRvT7SVdmV6RCCy\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 281px;\" \/><\/div>","QuestionJS":"Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnReady(function () {\n  var phase = Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(\"phase\") || \"\";\n\n  var key = \"counted_\" + this.questionId;\n  if (Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(key) === \"1\") return;\n\n  function inc(doneKey, totalKey){\n    var done  = parseInt(Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(doneKey)  || \"0\", 10);\n    var total = parseInt(Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.getEmbeddedData(totalKey) || \"1\", 10);\n    total = Math.max(total, 1);\n    done = Math.min(done + 1, total);\n    Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(doneKey, String(done));\n  }\n\n  if (phase === \"norming\") inc(\"norm_done\", \"norm_total\");\n  if (phase === \"memory\")  inc(\"mem_done\",  \"mem_total\");\n\n  Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData(key, \"1\");\n});","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":" ","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":37,"NextAnswerId":1,"Graphics":"IM_e3tZiBPIiiVzzE1","GraphicsDescription":"wm1659c.jpg","QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https:\/\/virginia.az1.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_ag6DK3heLwAMEyG\" style=\"width: 399px; height: 280px;\" \/><\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q1212","QuestionID":"QID1212"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_aUYX8XjalY6EcDk","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1213","SecondaryAttribute":"How positive (pleasant) or negative (unpleasant) does the person in this image appear to be feeli...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">How <b>positive<